1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:03,960
[Six Months Ago]

2
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:41,000
You've been standing outside

3
00:00:43,130 --> 00:00:44,060
for four minutes and 20 seconds.

4
00:00:44,530 --> 00:00:45,860
How did you know?

5
00:00:46,330 --> 00:00:47,560
I saw your shadow under the door.

6
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:27,560
Relax. There aren't any cameras here.

7
00:01:27,700 --> 00:01:29,260
No security cameras downstairs either.

8
00:01:30,030 --> 00:01:32,100
Every store on this street is run-down.

9
00:01:32,530 --> 00:01:35,430
Relax. No one will know you were here.

10
00:01:36,230 --> 00:01:37,100
My assistant knows.

11
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:40,700
I didn't tell him why I came up.

12
00:01:41,530 --> 00:01:43,660
How do I know you won't tell anyone?

13
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:49,500
Hey, I ran into Hui Loek To on the street!

14
00:01:49,530 --> 00:01:50,960
I even invited him over.

15
00:01:52,700 --> 00:01:53,530
Are you crazy?

16
00:01:58,530 --> 00:02:00,200
Why so nervous, To?

17
00:02:12,100 --> 00:02:13,600
Your first time?

18
00:02:15,930 --> 00:02:17,300
Are you done asking?

19
00:02:24,530 --> 00:02:26,260
If you're uncomfortable,

20
00:02:27,630 --> 00:02:28,900
you can leave anytime.

21
00:02:30,930 --> 00:02:32,060
No one's keeping you here.

22
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:39,300
What, you think

23
00:02:40,530 --> 00:02:41,760
anyone could keep me here?

24
00:02:44,900 --> 00:02:45,900
I don't know.

25
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:47,700
Want to find out?

26
00:02:51,230 --> 00:02:52,130
Any way I want?

27
00:02:56,700 --> 00:02:58,400
How do you want to try?

28
00:05:03,660 --> 00:05:05,130
You okay?

29
00:05:05,630 --> 00:05:06,860
If you don't like it,

30
00:05:07,500 --> 00:05:08,900
we can stop anytime.

31
00:05:11,900 --> 00:05:12,730
Stop?

32
00:07:18,520 --> 00:07:21,260
♪With you, it's like I can breathe again♪

33
00:07:21,690 --> 00:07:24,460
♪I can't live without this breath, this heartbeat♪

34
00:07:24,580 --> 00:07:27,370
♪Forever's too far, but you're right here♪

35
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:29,800
♪Together we'll take on this jaded world♪

36
00:07:29,940 --> 00:07:32,780
♪With you, I'll cross the dark, outrun the pain, and run away♪

37
00:07:32,860 --> 00:07:36,940
♪Still believing in true love, no matter how naive, calling you♪

38
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:41,730
♪I'm willing to wait♪

39
00:07:42,580 --> 00:07:45,420
♪I love you like you're a part of me♪

40
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:48,220
♪I want to share my life with you♪

41
00:07:48,860 --> 00:07:54,640
♪To love this deeply, I'll give a little more♪

42
00:07:54,990 --> 00:07:56,790
♪In this cold and gray city♪

43
00:07:56,870 --> 00:07:58,500
♪Through all the pain, I'll hold you. Is it true?♪

44
00:07:58,600 --> 00:08:00,950
♪Pieces of our memories slowly fade♪

45
00:08:01,030 --> 00:08:01,610
♪Stay with me♪

46
00:08:01,750 --> 00:08:04,360
♪Do you remember the day we crossed paths?♪

47
00:08:04,440 --> 00:08:05,140
♪Stay with me♪

48
00:08:05,220 --> 00:08:08,060
♪Do you remember the forever we promised?♪

49
00:08:08,550 --> 00:08:10,560
♪Who's waiting for you to save them?♪

50
00:08:11,090 --> 00:08:13,600
♪My heart aches, breaks, and struggles on♪

51
00:08:14,130 --> 00:08:16,640
♪How can I hold on to everything in one moment?♪

52
00:08:17,360 --> 00:08:20,860
♪Stop blaming fate and learn to let it be♪

53
00:08:22,700 --> 00:08:24,700
[Ash]
[Episode 2]

54
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:26,890
There are cops here.

55
00:08:27,460 --> 00:08:31,030
- Cops!
- Police busted a drug deal last night.

56
00:08:31,060 --> 00:08:34,360
Several suspected ringleaders were arrested.

57
00:08:34,630 --> 00:08:38,860
- Police killed suspected dealers.
- Cops!

58
00:08:38,860 --> 00:08:41,930
Another key member, known as Keung,

59
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:43,490
was shot and went missing at sea.

60
00:08:43,860 --> 00:08:46,760
Police divers are searching for him.

61
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:05,300
[Chief Inspector of Police, Kowloon East Regional Crime Unit, Fung Hong Man]

62
00:09:05,330 --> 00:09:06,760
[Death Confirmation Report]
Since Cheung Wai Keung is dead,

63
00:09:07,730 --> 00:09:08,760
we'll close and archive the case.

64
00:09:09,860 --> 00:09:11,290
I've got a new assignment for you.

65
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:12,760
Yes, sir! Thank you, sir!

66
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:16,560
Come in!

67
00:09:18,930 --> 00:09:19,760
Hey, Officer Chan!

68
00:09:22,560 --> 00:09:23,660
What's going on?

69
00:09:23,890 --> 00:09:25,360
We just finished our briefing.

70
00:09:25,690 --> 00:09:27,830
Already here to steal my guy? You're eager.

71
00:09:27,930 --> 00:09:29,060
Of course.

72
00:09:29,290 --> 00:09:31,690
I heard our rising star is finally free.

73
00:09:31,730 --> 00:09:33,330
So I came right over to steal him from you.

74
00:09:34,130 --> 00:09:35,560
Fei Foon, let me introduce you.

75
00:09:35,560 --> 00:09:37,490
Officer Chan, Commercial Crime Bureau.

76
00:09:37,760 --> 00:09:38,930
Good afternoon, sir!

77
00:09:39,090 --> 00:09:39,890
Very polite.

78
00:09:41,490 --> 00:09:44,230
Tall, handsome, and capable.

79
00:09:44,460 --> 00:09:47,290
Quite the star. You've got a bright future.

80
00:09:47,490 --> 00:09:48,360
Thank you, sir.

81
00:09:48,360 --> 00:09:49,930
Just don't fall for me too quickly.

82
00:09:50,190 --> 00:09:52,390
You haven't even seen my best qualities yet, sir.

83
00:09:53,560 --> 00:09:54,930
That's a lot of confidence.

84
00:09:56,460 --> 00:09:57,760
Confidence is a good thing.

85
00:09:58,090 --> 00:09:59,760
Welcome to the Commercial Crime Bureau.

86
00:10:00,060 --> 00:10:01,090
Can't wait to see what you can do.

87
00:10:01,760 --> 00:10:02,560
Thank you, sir.

88
00:10:03,260 --> 00:10:05,090
I won't let you down, Officer Chan.

89
00:10:05,260 --> 00:10:07,290
Uh-oh. I think I'm falling for you already.

90
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:14,130
Please do me a favor.

91
00:10:15,930 --> 00:10:16,730
Coming.

92
00:10:55,560 --> 00:10:56,890
What are you taking pictures of?

93
00:10:57,460 --> 00:10:59,760
You. I took some pictures of you sleeping.

94
00:11:02,560 --> 00:11:04,190
Why are you taking pictures of me?

95
00:11:04,360 --> 00:11:05,090
Am I not allowed to?

96
00:11:06,430 --> 00:11:06,930
Let me see.

97
00:11:06,930 --> 00:11:08,790
Fine, I'll show you.

98
00:11:10,360 --> 00:11:11,230
Look how handsome you are.

99
00:11:12,560 --> 00:11:15,060
Hey, don't take pictures of me in bed.

100
00:11:15,090 --> 00:11:16,230
They're not bedroom pics.

101
00:11:20,360 --> 00:11:20,890
Well?

102
00:11:20,930 --> 00:11:22,190
Want to take one together?

103
00:11:25,360 --> 00:11:26,090
I'll do it.

104
00:11:37,560 --> 00:11:39,130
Why'd you bite me?

105
00:12:07,290 --> 00:12:08,090
That's everything.

106
00:12:08,660 --> 00:12:09,460
Thanks, man.

107
00:12:21,960 --> 00:12:23,260
Hey, Dickson.

108
00:12:24,130 --> 00:12:25,430
Long time no see.

109
00:12:25,460 --> 00:12:27,290
Thought you ditched us after changing jobs.

110
00:12:27,660 --> 00:12:28,930
I've just been busy lately.

111
00:12:28,930 --> 00:12:29,760
I'd never ditch this place.

112
00:12:30,260 --> 00:12:30,930
The usual.

113
00:12:31,530 --> 00:12:32,330
Wait.

114
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:36,490
You got any smoky whiskey?

115
00:12:36,830 --> 00:12:38,160
Come on, don't mess with me.

116
00:12:38,160 --> 00:12:40,490
You think I carry fancy stuff like that?

117
00:12:40,530 --> 00:12:41,730
Regular whiskey okay?

118
00:12:41,860 --> 00:12:43,130
That'll do.

119
00:12:47,130 --> 00:12:47,760
What's wrong?

120
00:12:47,760 --> 00:12:50,060
You look like things aren't going your way.

121
00:12:50,860 --> 00:12:51,790
I'm fine.

122
00:12:51,830 --> 00:12:53,160
Work's been

123
00:12:53,830 --> 00:12:54,930
going pretty well lately.

124
00:12:55,690 --> 00:12:57,130
I'm not talking about work.

125
00:12:57,930 --> 00:12:59,830
Guys only get this worked up over a few things.

126
00:13:00,190 --> 00:13:01,090
Whiskey.

127
00:13:02,090 --> 00:13:03,360
You don't miss a thing.

128
00:13:04,860 --> 00:13:06,560
I brought this on myself.

129
00:13:06,730 --> 00:13:09,060
I thought he was fun, so I made the first move.

130
00:13:10,890 --> 00:13:12,690
Turns out I was the one who started it,

131
00:13:13,730 --> 00:13:15,330
and I'm the one who fell for him.

132
00:13:16,530 --> 00:13:18,560
I kept telling myself not to get attached.

133
00:13:20,090 --> 00:13:21,430
Does he treat you well?

134
00:13:22,930 --> 00:13:24,860
We usually get along pretty well.

135
00:13:25,490 --> 00:13:26,230
No.

136
00:13:26,530 --> 00:13:27,330
More like,

137
00:13:27,330 --> 00:13:29,960
we get along when he's in a good mood.

138
00:13:32,090 --> 00:13:34,630
The rest of the time, it's always his way.

139
00:13:35,530 --> 00:13:37,560
He never asks what I want.

140
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:39,460
He's the worst.

141
00:13:39,930 --> 00:13:41,430
It's actually pretty simple.

142
00:13:41,690 --> 00:13:43,730
If you can't take it and you're miserable,

143
00:13:43,730 --> 00:13:44,960
then leave.

144
00:13:45,490 --> 00:13:47,330
Why stay with someone who doesn't care about you

145
00:13:47,330 --> 00:13:49,160
and just keeps draining you? Right?

146
00:13:49,160 --> 00:13:50,560
He's not worth it.

147
00:13:51,860 --> 00:13:54,360
I thought I could just walk away too.

148
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:56,290
But it's not that simple.

149
00:13:57,090 --> 00:13:57,890
True.

150
00:13:58,130 --> 00:13:59,860
Otherwise, you wouldn't have come here alone

151
00:13:59,930 --> 00:14:00,960
to drink with me, right?

152
00:14:01,290 --> 00:14:02,930
Cheers.

153
00:14:03,130 --> 00:14:04,460
Oh, shut up.

154
00:14:09,160 --> 00:14:11,660
So, got any advice?

155
00:14:12,060 --> 00:14:14,760
You're giving me the question of the century.

156
00:14:15,430 --> 00:14:16,560
How about this?

157
00:14:16,560 --> 00:14:18,190
Try something.

158
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:20,860
See if he actually cares about you.

159
00:14:21,660 --> 00:14:23,290
If he does,

160
00:14:23,290 --> 00:14:24,530
he'll change on his own.

161
00:14:24,930 --> 00:14:26,530
If you test him and he doesn't react,

162
00:14:26,890 --> 00:14:27,960
Break up with him.

163
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:29,090
Dump him.

164
00:14:31,490 --> 00:14:32,560
Makes sense.

165
00:14:34,360 --> 00:14:35,860
But sometimes I'm scared

166
00:14:36,090 --> 00:14:39,130
I won't like the answer I get.

167
00:14:39,660 --> 00:14:40,990
What's there to be scared of?

168
00:14:41,560 --> 00:14:43,390
There's nothing a glass of whiskey can't fix.

169
00:14:43,560 --> 00:14:44,790
And if that doesn't work,

170
00:14:45,360 --> 00:14:46,760
have a few more.

171
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:47,630
Right?

172
00:14:52,930 --> 00:14:54,130
Thanks.

173
00:14:57,060 --> 00:14:58,290
Think it over.

174
00:18:20,460 --> 00:18:21,260
Who are you?

175
00:18:21,260 --> 00:18:22,260
Why are you following me?

176
00:18:23,330 --> 00:18:24,430
Police. I'm going to search you.

177
00:18:24,740 --> 00:18:26,440
Sir, please cooperate.

178
00:18:26,460 --> 00:18:27,430
[Mok Fei Foon, Sergeant]

179
00:18:31,930 --> 00:18:33,660
Forgot me already?

180
00:18:38,960 --> 00:18:40,290
What are you playing at?

181
00:18:40,860 --> 00:18:41,730
Messing with me?

182
00:18:42,490 --> 00:18:43,260
To.

183
00:18:43,730 --> 00:18:45,660
You know that's assaulting an officer.

184
00:18:45,760 --> 00:18:47,490
You'd better be gentle.

185
00:19:03,560 --> 00:19:04,330
That's all?

186
00:19:05,030 --> 00:19:06,330
I was actually looking forward to it.

187
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:09,760
Keys.

188
00:19:10,260 --> 00:19:11,430
Hand them over.

189
00:19:14,490 --> 00:19:15,530
Can't find them.

190
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:19,890
Give me the keys. Now.

191
00:19:24,030 --> 00:19:25,160
Haven't seen you in a while.

192
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:26,560
You're a lot bolder now.

193
00:20:59,730 --> 00:21:01,160
When you first approached me,

194
00:21:02,590 --> 00:21:03,890
was it because you were investigating me?

195
00:21:04,860 --> 00:21:06,190
Is there something about you I should investigate?

196
00:21:11,730 --> 00:21:13,730
You know Cheung Wai Keung is dead.

197
00:21:14,030 --> 00:21:14,760
So?

198
00:21:14,930 --> 00:21:17,930
So don't come looking for me at that place anymore.

199
00:21:22,260 --> 00:21:23,730
Did I say I wanted to keep seeing you?

200
00:21:25,330 --> 00:21:26,230
What?

201
00:21:26,490 --> 00:21:28,360
Being a cop scares you?

202
00:21:34,190 --> 00:21:36,390
Or do you only like guys like Cheung Wai Keung

203
00:21:36,690 --> 00:21:38,490
because they're easier to control?

204
00:21:39,260 --> 00:21:40,730
Say whatever you want.

205
00:21:48,490 --> 00:21:49,760
Do you still want to keep this going?

206
00:21:51,490 --> 00:21:52,260
No.

207
00:21:56,090 --> 00:21:57,160
Why?

208
00:22:01,260 --> 00:22:03,030
Then what was that just now?

209
00:22:04,760 --> 00:22:06,360
You came to me.

210
00:22:32,860 --> 00:22:34,390
Come over. Let me introduce you.

211
00:22:35,030 --> 00:22:36,330
I want you to meet our new guy.

212
00:22:36,330 --> 00:22:37,090
Come on.

213
00:22:37,930 --> 00:22:38,790
Mok Fei Foon.

214
00:22:38,930 --> 00:22:40,760
He's joining our Commercial Crime Bureau today.

215
00:22:41,490 --> 00:22:42,430
Introduce yourself.

216
00:22:42,830 --> 00:22:43,460
Hey, everyone.

217
00:22:43,460 --> 00:22:44,590
Just call me Foon.

218
00:22:45,360 --> 00:22:46,890
Let me introduce everyone.

219
00:22:47,160 --> 00:22:49,490
Pang, Siu Kit, Ping, and On.

220
00:22:49,930 --> 00:22:51,330
And this is Joseph.

221
00:22:51,460 --> 00:22:52,730
He's new here too.

222
00:22:53,160 --> 00:22:53,730
Nice to meet you, Officer Mok.

223
00:22:53,760 --> 00:22:54,560
I'm Joseph.

224
00:22:54,760 --> 00:22:55,760
If I ever mess something up

225
00:22:55,760 --> 00:22:56,760
or do something wrong,

226
00:22:56,760 --> 00:22:57,790
just tell me straight.

227
00:22:57,890 --> 00:22:58,790
You can even chew me out.

228
00:22:58,830 --> 00:22:59,730
I'm always willing to learn.

229
00:23:01,760 --> 00:23:02,590
No problem.

230
00:23:02,590 --> 00:23:03,230
No need to be so formal.

231
00:23:03,260 --> 00:23:04,590
We'll learn from each other.

232
00:23:05,430 --> 00:23:06,190
Alright.

233
00:23:06,190 --> 00:23:07,490
He's fresh out of the academy

234
00:23:07,530 --> 00:23:08,260
and still pretty green.

235
00:23:08,290 --> 00:23:09,730
Keep an eye on him for me.

236
00:23:09,960 --> 00:23:10,760
Okay?

237
00:23:11,190 --> 00:23:12,330
Now that everyone's met,

238
00:23:12,360 --> 00:23:13,590
let's get to work.

239
00:23:18,030 --> 00:23:19,030
Looks like a big case.

240
00:23:19,430 --> 00:23:20,290
Yeah.

241
00:23:20,290 --> 00:23:22,160
You got a big one on your first day.

242
00:23:22,330 --> 00:23:24,330
According to Interpol,

243
00:23:24,530 --> 00:23:26,990
for the past year, a group called Dreamweaver

244
00:23:27,090 --> 00:23:28,590
has been running a global counterfeiting ring,

245
00:23:28,730 --> 00:23:31,190
[Counterfeit Currencies: HKD, MOP]
producing fake currencies worldwide.

246
00:23:31,590 --> 00:23:35,460
[Japanese Yen]
Worth tens of billions of dollars.

247
00:23:36,160 --> 00:23:37,330
Their crimes

248
00:23:37,360 --> 00:23:39,990
span Europe, the Americas, and even Asia.

249
00:23:40,490 --> 00:23:41,590
According to our intel,

250
00:23:41,590 --> 00:23:43,290
they may already be in Hong Kong, China.

251
00:23:50,690 --> 00:23:51,890
These are really well made.

252
00:23:53,090 --> 00:23:54,760
Even I can't tell they're fake.

253
00:23:55,360 --> 00:23:56,590
It's not just you.

254
00:24:04,360 --> 00:24:06,090
Even counterfeit detectors can't spot them.

255
00:24:06,590 --> 00:24:08,260
I've had several banks test them.

256
00:24:08,430 --> 00:24:09,330
Only the latest

257
00:24:09,330 --> 00:24:10,730
counterfeit detectors can spot

258
00:24:10,730 --> 00:24:11,790
the difference.

259
00:24:11,930 --> 00:24:13,990
But most places don't have equipment that advanced.

260
00:24:14,030 --> 00:24:14,760
Right?

261
00:24:16,090 --> 00:24:17,660
We've had several reports recently.

262
00:24:18,160 --> 00:24:19,790
Banks across Hong Kong, China

263
00:24:19,830 --> 00:24:22,030
have been receiving these new counterfeit bills.

264
00:24:22,490 --> 00:24:24,160
But according to our intel,

265
00:24:24,360 --> 00:24:26,660
there are two major channels for counterfeit money here.

266
00:24:27,160 --> 00:24:30,260
[Operation Gutenberg]
First is the old Eastern Hall gang.

267
00:24:30,860 --> 00:24:33,130
Their main business in Southeast Asia

268
00:24:33,130 --> 00:24:34,190
is arms trafficking.

269
00:24:34,760 --> 00:24:36,890
[Ho Tung Fong]
They found out during an earlier deal

270
00:24:36,930 --> 00:24:38,360
they'd paid with counterfeit bills.

271
00:24:38,760 --> 00:24:39,660
And it was a large amount.

272
00:24:40,090 --> 00:24:42,660
So they likely got the bills from Dreamweaver.

273
00:24:43,930 --> 00:24:44,960
The second channel

274
00:24:46,360 --> 00:24:47,460
is Sheng Tung's uncle,

275
00:24:48,360 --> 00:24:49,160
To Si Hong.

276
00:24:49,180 --> 00:24:50,090
[To Si Hong]

277
00:24:50,090 --> 00:24:51,560
According to overseas intel,

278
00:24:51,690 --> 00:24:54,130
he's used counterfeit bills at several casinos.

279
00:24:54,360 --> 00:24:56,590
He's been identified and blacklisted for a while.

280
00:24:56,760 --> 00:24:58,760
To Si Hong is currently in Hong Kong, China.

281
00:24:59,330 --> 00:25:00,760
We plan to start with him.

282
00:25:02,360 --> 00:25:03,490
Foon, you're taking this lead.

283
00:25:03,760 --> 00:25:04,590
Understood, sir.

284
00:25:04,960 --> 00:25:06,190
Officer Mok needs a partner too.

285
00:25:06,260 --> 00:25:07,890
Can I go with him?

286
00:25:10,030 --> 00:25:10,730
Alright.

287
00:25:11,190 --> 00:25:13,390
You'll learn a lot working with a veteran.

288
00:25:14,190 --> 00:25:15,490
Everyone, move fast.

289
00:25:15,560 --> 00:25:16,330
Make sure you note the key details.

290
00:25:16,560 --> 00:25:18,590
We'll meet with Interpol online shortly

291
00:25:18,590 --> 00:25:19,690
to get the latest on their investigation.

292
00:25:20,160 --> 00:25:20,990
If they make any move,

293
00:25:21,030 --> 00:25:22,190
we'll give them our full support.

294
00:25:22,360 --> 00:25:24,760
We have to catch the mastermind behind Dreamweaver.

295
00:25:25,030 --> 00:25:25,590
Clear?

296
00:25:25,590 --> 00:25:26,290
Yes, sir!

297
00:25:27,030 --> 00:25:28,290
I'll go get things ready for the meeting.

298
00:25:30,360 --> 00:25:31,760
Officer Mok, I look forward to learning from you.

299
00:25:32,190 --> 00:25:33,660
If I mess up, just set me straight.

300
00:25:34,360 --> 00:25:35,290
No problem.

301
00:25:35,730 --> 00:25:36,360
Good.

302
00:25:39,100 --> 00:25:41,460
[Golden Dream Nightclub]

303
00:25:41,460 --> 00:25:44,070
[Golden Treasure Karaoke Nightclub]

304
00:25:49,880 --> 00:25:51,780
[Harbour Crystal Centre]

305
00:26:05,460 --> 00:26:07,730
I told you to wash the car, not stare at it.

306
00:26:08,730 --> 00:26:11,230
Look busy doing your own thing

307
00:26:11,460 --> 00:26:13,590
while keeping a close eye on the target.

308
00:26:13,890 --> 00:26:14,930
Got it?

309
00:26:15,960 --> 00:26:17,230
Sorry. I'm a little nervous.

310
00:26:17,760 --> 00:26:19,160
Don't apologize to me.

311
00:26:19,160 --> 00:26:20,160
If this goes sideways,

312
00:26:20,160 --> 00:26:21,160
you're taking the fall.

313
00:26:21,190 --> 00:26:21,990
What?

314
00:26:22,490 --> 00:26:23,990
Don't "what" me. Keep washing.

315
00:26:34,560 --> 00:26:35,260
Officer Mok.

316
00:26:35,660 --> 00:26:36,790
That's a nice lighter.

317
00:26:36,830 --> 00:26:37,730
Where'd you get it?

318
00:26:37,930 --> 00:26:38,990
We're working.

319
00:26:39,030 --> 00:26:41,190
Stay focused. No irrelevant questions.

320
00:26:43,760 --> 00:26:45,830
What do you think To Si Hong is doing here?

321
00:26:47,190 --> 00:26:48,190
Based on the intel,

322
00:26:48,490 --> 00:26:50,560
this is probably an illegal casino.

323
00:26:50,730 --> 00:26:52,830
No surprise he'd come here to scam some money.

324
00:26:53,760 --> 00:26:54,260
Officer Mok.

325
00:26:54,360 --> 00:26:55,960
You really know your stuff. That's impressive.

326
00:26:56,360 --> 00:26:57,630
This is basic stuff.

327
00:26:58,190 --> 00:26:59,590
You should've learned plenty at the academy.

328
00:27:01,460 --> 00:27:03,590
My academy instructors weren't as good as you.

329
00:27:03,590 --> 00:27:04,990
They couldn't teach real field experience.

330
00:27:05,360 --> 00:27:06,990
You can't say that.

331
00:27:08,890 --> 00:27:10,330
Most of what your instructors teach you

332
00:27:10,330 --> 00:27:11,590
is how to stay alive.

333
00:27:12,060 --> 00:27:13,690
Apologize to them right now.

334
00:27:14,030 --> 00:27:14,690
Now?

335
00:27:14,690 --> 00:27:15,330
Right now.

336
00:27:15,330 --> 00:27:16,990
Apologize while you wash the car.

337
00:27:17,190 --> 00:27:18,230
Pick up the pace.

338
00:27:19,260 --> 00:27:20,760
Or I'm leaving you here after the shift.

339
00:27:21,190 --> 00:27:21,990
Okay.

340
00:27:22,190 --> 00:27:23,230
Sorry, sir.

341
00:27:23,930 --> 00:27:24,990
Sorry, sir.

342
00:27:25,360 --> 00:27:27,590
Sorry, sir.

343
00:27:35,590 --> 00:27:37,430
They're not even trying out there.

344
00:27:38,030 --> 00:27:40,360
Exactly. They can barely stay on their feet.

345
00:27:40,360 --> 00:27:43,860
What are they doing? Still no goal!

346
00:27:44,190 --> 00:27:46,230
Next bet's on the home team to score. Go!

347
00:27:47,190 --> 00:27:48,660
Hurry up!

348
00:27:57,290 --> 00:27:58,160
Place the bet.

349
00:27:58,430 --> 00:27:59,290
50,000.

350
00:28:19,130 --> 00:28:19,930
Vincent.

351
00:28:20,190 --> 00:28:21,690
Vincent, let me explain.

352
00:28:21,860 --> 00:28:22,760
Just hear me out.

353
00:28:22,760 --> 00:28:23,790
Please, let me explain first.

354
00:28:28,060 --> 00:28:28,860
Uncle To.

355
00:28:30,460 --> 00:28:31,890
I let it slide when you were making money on the side.

356
00:28:32,190 --> 00:28:33,590
I didn't hold it against you.

357
00:28:35,490 --> 00:28:37,230
But you scammed money from our own operation.

358
00:28:38,890 --> 00:28:40,190
I know I messed up!

359
00:28:40,190 --> 00:28:41,460
I just wasn't thinking straight!

360
00:28:41,830 --> 00:28:43,190
It was a stupid mistake!

361
00:28:44,330 --> 00:28:45,360
How much is left?

362
00:28:45,760 --> 00:28:46,560
I spent it all.

363
00:28:46,760 --> 00:28:48,060
Nothing's left. Not a cent.

364
00:28:53,030 --> 00:28:54,460
Don't lie to me!

365
00:28:54,660 --> 00:28:55,930
Where'd you get those counterfeit bills?

366
00:28:56,890 --> 00:28:57,690
Well...

367
00:28:57,760 --> 00:28:59,090
A contact hooked me up

368
00:28:59,130 --> 00:29:00,460
with a friend who supplied them.

369
00:29:00,690 --> 00:29:02,990
You just borrowed money from the gang

370
00:29:03,030 --> 00:29:04,060
because you said you were short on cash.

371
00:29:04,060 --> 00:29:05,730
So where'd you get that much money?

372
00:29:11,760 --> 00:29:13,160
Talk!

373
00:29:16,930 --> 00:29:18,330
I know I messed up.

374
00:29:18,730 --> 00:29:20,730
I got greedy.

375
00:29:20,730 --> 00:29:21,590
I'm sorry.

376
00:29:21,590 --> 00:29:22,890
I know you messed up.

377
00:29:24,190 --> 00:29:25,190
The gang left

378
00:29:25,190 --> 00:29:26,260
over three million with you.

379
00:29:26,530 --> 00:29:27,930
Is that money still there?

380
00:29:29,030 --> 00:29:30,460
I'm sorry.

381
00:29:31,490 --> 00:29:32,330
I'm sorry.

382
00:29:32,330 --> 00:29:33,490
I won't do it again.

383
00:29:33,530 --> 00:29:34,460
Never again.

384
00:29:34,490 --> 00:29:35,260
Uncle To.

385
00:29:35,930 --> 00:29:37,490
You've been with Sheng Tung for years.

386
00:29:37,530 --> 00:29:39,060
You know the rules.

387
00:29:39,090 --> 00:29:41,630
The rules? No!

388
00:29:41,660 --> 00:29:45,730
Vincent, no!

389
00:29:45,760 --> 00:29:47,490
Fung, no!

390
00:29:47,690 --> 00:29:48,730
Vincent!

391
00:29:57,560 --> 00:29:59,060
Take him to Dr. Chan.

392
00:30:00,090 --> 00:30:00,960
Wait!

393
00:30:21,130 --> 00:30:23,390
Find out who he's been in contact with lately.

394
00:30:24,060 --> 00:30:26,690
You don't usually go this far.

395
00:30:27,730 --> 00:30:28,930
Why are you so worked up?

396
00:30:29,560 --> 00:30:32,630
Guys like him don't matter if they die.

397
00:30:33,490 --> 00:30:34,260
Then

398
00:30:34,830 --> 00:30:36,490
whose death would matter?

399
00:30:45,960 --> 00:30:47,890
Two guys outside are acting suspicious.

400
00:30:48,330 --> 00:30:49,390
Want me to check them out?

401
00:30:54,090 --> 00:30:56,190
Tell the guys outside to stay sharp, just in case.

402
00:30:57,260 --> 00:30:58,030
And...

403
00:30:59,060 --> 00:31:00,730
Find out what those two are investigating.

404
00:31:01,060 --> 00:31:03,530
If you're worried about him, just call him.

405
00:31:04,090 --> 00:31:05,130
Why do you always make me check on him?

406
00:31:05,130 --> 00:31:06,560
I call you all the time too.

407
00:31:06,830 --> 00:31:08,490
Does that mean I'm worried about you?

408
00:31:09,030 --> 00:31:10,960
I already know you care about me.

409
00:31:11,590 --> 00:31:13,430
Always working late, keeping me by your side.

410
00:31:13,830 --> 00:31:15,060
But we can never be together.

411
00:31:15,660 --> 00:31:16,660
Just let me go.

412
00:31:19,190 --> 00:31:19,990
Go.

413
00:31:20,730 --> 00:31:21,790
You talk too much.

414
00:31:23,590 --> 00:31:24,390
Sorry, sir.

415
00:31:26,560 --> 00:31:27,460
Sorry, sir.

416
00:31:28,590 --> 00:31:29,430
Sorry, sir.

417
00:31:42,330 --> 00:31:43,460
Careful!

418
00:31:50,890 --> 00:31:52,430
Officer Mok, are you okay?

419
00:31:52,460 --> 00:31:53,260
I'm fine.

420
00:31:53,590 --> 00:31:56,060
Run XW2927.

421
00:31:56,560 --> 00:31:58,560
What's XW2927?

422
00:32:01,060 --> 00:32:02,260
The license plate!

423
00:32:03,590 --> 00:32:05,390
You really worry me sometimes.

424
00:32:06,690 --> 00:32:07,890
Officer Mok, you're bleeding.

425
00:32:07,890 --> 00:32:09,090
Want me to bandage it?

426
00:32:10,890 --> 00:32:12,530
Help me back so you can bandage me.

427
00:32:12,890 --> 00:32:14,430
And maybe get your head checked while we're at it.

428
00:32:15,430 --> 00:32:18,730
Careful.

429
00:32:18,730 --> 00:32:20,060
I'm fine.

430
00:32:20,460 --> 00:32:22,190
Careful. Hold on.

431
00:32:22,490 --> 00:32:24,190
Careful. Hold on.

432
00:32:29,760 --> 00:32:30,660
Alright.

433
00:32:30,690 --> 00:32:33,990
- I know. - Careful.

434
00:32:43,430 --> 00:32:44,760
Why is this taking so long?

435
00:32:45,060 --> 00:32:46,560
I'm afraid I'll hurt you.

436
00:32:47,130 --> 00:32:48,560
All done. Let's get back to work.

437
00:32:49,190 --> 00:32:50,790
Officer Mok, don't you need to rest?

438
00:32:51,860 --> 00:32:53,030
Don't you have work to do?

439
00:32:53,530 --> 00:32:55,030
Did you finish the report?

440
00:32:55,530 --> 00:32:56,990
Did you run the plate?

441
00:32:57,560 --> 00:32:59,390
Or were you planning to let AI do it for you?

442
00:33:00,190 --> 00:33:01,630
I'll finish it in a bit.

443
00:33:05,360 --> 00:33:06,230
Officer Mok, you're leaving?

444
00:33:06,830 --> 00:33:08,430
We're done for today.

445
00:33:08,830 --> 00:33:10,260
Why don't I drive you home?

446
00:33:10,460 --> 00:33:11,890
You did just get hurt.

447
00:33:15,460 --> 00:33:17,190
What? Is there something on my face?

448
00:33:17,760 --> 00:33:18,890
Sometimes I really wonder

449
00:33:19,560 --> 00:33:21,490
if you actually want to be a cop.

450
00:33:21,890 --> 00:33:23,690
Your work isn't done and you're ready to leave.

451
00:33:24,460 --> 00:33:25,390
But you...

452
00:33:27,890 --> 00:33:28,960
Don't worry about me.

453
00:33:30,560 --> 00:33:32,730
It's just my hand. I won't die.

454
00:33:33,190 --> 00:33:34,490
Stop hovering over me.

455
00:33:34,930 --> 00:33:36,660
Finish up and go home early.

456
00:33:37,530 --> 00:33:38,360
See you tomorrow.

457
00:33:50,960 --> 00:33:51,760
Seriously?

458
00:34:00,530 --> 00:34:01,590
What are you doing here?

459
00:34:02,030 --> 00:34:03,260
Were you following me?

460
00:34:03,260 --> 00:34:04,030
Yeah.

461
00:34:04,190 --> 00:34:05,590
You've been messing with me this whole time.

462
00:34:06,260 --> 00:34:07,490
You think I'm just going to let that slide?

463
00:34:07,490 --> 00:34:08,130
You...

464
00:34:12,260 --> 00:34:14,490
I've slept less than six hours total these past few days.

465
00:34:14,490 --> 00:34:15,860
I'm not in the mood for your games.

466
00:34:16,760 --> 00:34:17,790
Give me back my key.

467
00:34:28,190 --> 00:34:29,390
Why are you still standing there?

468
00:34:29,690 --> 00:34:30,990
Waiting to see when you'd go home.

469
00:34:31,430 --> 00:34:33,560
Whether I go home is none of your business.

470
00:34:35,730 --> 00:34:36,960
You look exhausted.

471
00:34:36,960 --> 00:34:37,760
I wanted to keep you company.

472
00:34:39,960 --> 00:34:41,990
I can handle things myself.

473
00:34:42,030 --> 00:34:43,130
You don't need to worry about me.

474
00:34:43,330 --> 00:34:44,630
I know you can handle it alone.

475
00:34:46,560 --> 00:34:47,390
But...

476
00:34:48,730 --> 00:34:50,330
You don't have to.

477
00:35:11,560 --> 00:35:12,730
Where's the bathroom?

478
00:35:18,130 --> 00:35:18,930
This way.

479
00:35:20,430 --> 00:35:21,760
Take a shower. Get in.

480
00:35:22,760 --> 00:35:24,560
Mr. Hui, I told you.

481
00:35:24,560 --> 00:35:26,290
I'm exhausted today.

482
00:35:26,730 --> 00:35:28,790
That's not what I meant.

483
00:35:40,430 --> 00:35:41,190
Get in.

484
00:35:42,960 --> 00:35:44,760
You want me in the tub with my clothes on?

485
00:35:45,360 --> 00:35:46,990
I said get in, so get in.

486
00:36:15,560 --> 00:36:16,730
Hey! Knock it off!

487
00:36:18,260 --> 00:36:19,430
Are you crazy?

488
00:36:27,160 --> 00:36:27,990
Awake now?

489
00:36:29,460 --> 00:36:30,790
Are you seeing someone else?

490
00:36:32,030 --> 00:36:33,360
What are you talking about?

491
00:36:34,060 --> 00:36:35,860
Some guy's been with you all day,

492
00:36:36,090 --> 00:36:37,490
getting all cozy with you.

493
00:36:38,030 --> 00:36:39,030
I haven't seen you for a few days,

494
00:36:40,260 --> 00:36:41,860
and you've already hooked him?

495
00:36:42,530 --> 00:36:44,030
So what if I have?

496
00:36:44,060 --> 00:36:45,330
None of your business!

497
00:36:47,560 --> 00:36:48,860
So you'll sleep with just anyone.

498
00:36:49,660 --> 00:36:51,390
Who I'm with

499
00:36:51,430 --> 00:36:52,460
and what we do

500
00:36:52,730 --> 00:36:54,360
is none of your business.

501
00:36:54,760 --> 00:36:56,030
Get out. Now!

502
00:36:56,430 --> 00:36:57,660
Don't make a mess of my place.

503
00:37:03,190 --> 00:37:04,790
I'm the only one you're allowed to have.

504
00:37:07,430 --> 00:37:09,460
You and I are over.

505
00:37:10,560 --> 00:37:11,790
We don't have to be.

506
00:37:12,060 --> 00:37:13,390
But you can't see anyone else.

507
00:37:13,930 --> 00:37:14,790
What did you say?

508
00:37:15,560 --> 00:37:17,390
You wanted to keep going in that alley, right?

509
00:37:18,360 --> 00:37:19,290
Now I'm saying yes.

510
00:37:19,330 --> 00:37:20,390
Do you have two personalities or something?

511
00:37:20,430 --> 00:37:21,430
You change your mind every five minutes.

512
00:37:21,490 --> 00:37:22,530
"Yes" or

513
00:37:22,530 --> 00:37:23,760
"No"?

514
00:37:23,930 --> 00:37:24,960
Don't waste my time.

515
00:37:26,430 --> 00:37:27,360
Well...

516
00:37:28,560 --> 00:37:29,730
No.

517
00:37:30,190 --> 00:37:30,990
Why?

518
00:37:31,960 --> 00:37:32,830
You think I'm stupid?

519
00:37:34,030 --> 00:37:35,660
First you said I threw myself at you.

520
00:37:36,830 --> 00:37:38,590
Then today you soaked me.

521
00:37:38,760 --> 00:37:40,190
You think I'd take you back?

522
00:37:41,330 --> 00:37:42,860
So you don't want to keep this going?

523
00:37:43,030 --> 00:37:43,660
Right.

524
00:37:46,060 --> 00:37:47,060
You want me to leave right now?

525
00:37:47,060 --> 00:37:47,730
Right.

526
00:37:49,560 --> 00:37:50,390
You said it.

527
00:38:24,330 --> 00:38:25,490
What are you trying to do now?

528
00:38:27,560 --> 00:38:28,330
I'll help you undress.

529
00:38:29,830 --> 00:38:31,430
Keep this nonsense up,

530
00:38:31,560 --> 00:38:33,460
and I'll charge you with trespassing!

531
00:38:33,490 --> 00:38:34,190
Fine.

532
00:38:39,760 --> 00:38:40,560
Take it off.

533
00:38:52,760 --> 00:38:53,560
Sit down.

534
00:38:59,190 --> 00:39:00,730
Sit. I'll wash your hair.

535
00:39:08,730 --> 00:39:09,790
To.

536
00:39:09,960 --> 00:39:11,830
Look at you. Not bad at all.

537
00:39:15,590 --> 00:39:17,290
When my little brother was a kid,

538
00:39:17,930 --> 00:39:19,660
I used to bathe him.

539
00:39:30,430 --> 00:39:31,190
Did your wound heal?

540
00:39:32,460 --> 00:39:33,290
What?

541
00:39:38,030 --> 00:39:38,760
Here.

542
00:39:40,560 --> 00:39:41,990
You got hit with an ashtray.

543
00:39:44,130 --> 00:39:45,430
It's nothing.

544
00:39:45,760 --> 00:39:47,430
My hair usually covers it,

545
00:39:47,460 --> 00:39:48,460
so you can't tell.

546
00:39:51,590 --> 00:39:52,390
I'm sorry.

547
00:39:56,290 --> 00:39:57,830
Why the long face?

548
00:39:59,360 --> 00:40:01,990
I won't let anything like that happen again.

549
00:40:34,160 --> 00:40:35,290
What's this supposed to mean?

550
00:40:35,690 --> 00:40:37,290
You said your counterfeit bills were top quality!

551
00:40:37,660 --> 00:40:38,760
So how did they get spotted?

552
00:40:39,190 --> 00:40:41,230
How much did you use at once?

553
00:40:41,530 --> 00:40:42,530
Yeah.

554
00:40:42,530 --> 00:40:44,260
I used them in large batches.

555
00:40:44,430 --> 00:40:46,160
Your bills are the problem here.

556
00:40:46,530 --> 00:40:47,760
If your product was good enough,

557
00:40:48,060 --> 00:40:49,190
it wouldn't matter how much I used!

558
00:40:49,560 --> 00:40:50,590
No matter how good the craftsmanship is,

559
00:40:50,760 --> 00:40:52,090
counterfeit money is still counterfeit.

560
00:40:52,660 --> 00:40:53,860
Using a large amount at once

561
00:40:54,190 --> 00:40:55,060
is bound to raise suspicion.

562
00:40:55,930 --> 00:40:57,360
Don't give me that garbage now!

563
00:40:57,430 --> 00:40:59,930
You used Sheng Tung's network to move them into Hong Kong, China.

564
00:41:00,130 --> 00:41:02,360
Now there's trouble, and you think you can just walk away?

